analysis with line transect cetacean data in which we are calculating seasonal abundances for two geographic strata for three species. We have nine surveys completed in different months of the year with very different amounts of\r\n effort for each month. I would like to use all pooled data by species for the detection functions and then subset the data for each species by area and season and stratify in dht2 using effort_sum = month to account for the variation in effort by month. We\r\n are under a time crunch and I know there were errors in the past with how the variance (ER) was calculated in past versions of distance using effort_sum. I&#39;m hoping someone can confirm that these errors have been corrected without me digging to far into the\r\n github. </div>\r\n<div>Thanks for any help or clarification you can provide. </div>\r\n<div>Janet Mossman </div>\r\n<p></p></div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/233607bd-2e28-4dde-a9a3-2018d8e8badcn%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/233607bd-2e28-4dde-a9a3-2018d8e8badcn%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471449739000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iSU45g81_8xD3gZQxb2Ey\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/233607bd-2e28-4dde-a9a3-2018d8e8badcn%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>"
